+### 5c.1 `phi-acyclic-copy-order` — three extra stack references in `rot()`
+
+Measured, three ways, all agreeing: `default 53 insns/5 stkref`,
+`CCC_EVICT_SHORT_K=0 52/5`, `legacy 68/28`. The pin (written 2026-09-27, 702
+commits before this round) wants `<=53` instructions **and `<=3` stack
+references**, plus `default <= escape-off`. Instruction count is within one of
+the pin; stack traffic is 2–3 references above it. Also re-measured with the
+newest upstream codegen commits reverted (`src/backend/state.rs`,
+`src/backend/x86/codegen/cast_ops.rs`): unchanged, so the drift is older than
+those merges. Nothing in this delivery touches the phi resolver, the escape
+policy or the allocator's slot classification, and the numbers are identical
+before and after it.
+
+This is therefore a real codegen regression someone introduced between
+2026-09-27 and this round — a rotation kernel spilling two to three more values
+than it should — and it should be *fixed*, not re-pinned. Next step: bisect
+`rot()`'s stack traffic over the 702 commits (`git bisect` on the instruction
+count is enough, the metric is deterministic and takes one `-O2 -S`).
+
+### 5c.2 `llvm-scalar-facts` — the hot-web steal never fires
+
+`CCC_NO_HOT_WEB_STEAL=1` produces byte-identical assembly for
+`tests/regression/hot_web_callee_saved.c`, i.e. the mechanism the gate exists to
+prove is inert on its own witness. Localised this session with temporary
+counters in `src/backend/regalloc/hot_web.rs` (since reverted; the file is
+untouched in this patch):
+
+```text
+phi_pairs=5 eligible=5 not_member=5 iv_shape=5        <- candidates exist
+cand v107 uses=310 assigned=false best=None           <- and are very hot
+avail=[1,2,3,4,5,6]  cand_bounds=Some((10,80))
+  reg 2: refused ["phi_pair"] holders=[109]           <- the only register holding a candidate's span
+```
+
+So the steal is reached, the candidate is hot (310 uses against a threshold of
+10), and every available register is rejected by one of the eviction guards —
+the visible one being `phi_pair_values.contains(holder)` on register 2's holder
+`v109`; the remaining registers are rejected by the cost comparison
+(`cost >= hot_count`) without a diagnostic. The fix needs a decision about
+which guard is now over-broad (most likely the phi-pair guard, which refuses
+*any* holder that is a phi pair, including loops where displacing it is what
+the pass was written for), and it must be measured on the corpus — the steal
+was tuned against gzip and the cmdline parser, so it can regress either way.
+
+Both items are recorded here rather than silently re-baselined, because a
+re-baseline would convert a real spilling regression and a dead optimisation
+into "expected".
